mbine two  tablespoons of chia seeds with quarter  cup of fresh or frozen blueberries have  a cup of milk and half a teaspoon of  vanilla  all you have to do is mix it up cover  and let it set overnight in the fridge  the next morning top it up with one  small sliced banana and two tablespoons  of pumpkin seeds I like to keep my  breakfast simple and I tend to make a  three or four bowls ahead  so this breakfast helps with my  digestion and I'm also getting more  berries and also fruits into my diet so  let me just add that in two fruits  serving checked s for lunch I wanted a  really simple Asian rice recipe which I  can prep ahead and bring it up with me  so I recreated a depend fried Indian  wild rice what you'll need are one cup  of cooked rice I used a mixture of brown  and white rice about one cup of sliced  zucchinis half a cup of broccoli cut  into small florets half a cup of carrots  sliced 2 spring onions sliced 1/2 a  tablespoon of oil about 3 tablespoons of  unsalted cashew nuts 2 tablespoons of  raisins 1 and 1/2 teaspoon of curry  powder and about half a cup of vegetable  stock so in a pot of boiling salted  water blanch the broccoli and carrots  for about 2 minutes drain and set aside  hits oil over medium-high heat stir in  the cashew nuts raisins and all the  vegetables saute for about 3 minutes and  stir in the spring onions curry powder  and cook for a couple more minutes then  pour in the vegetable stock and allowed  all the ingredients to simmer until the  vegetables are tender finally mix in the  rice remove from heat and serve so I'm  just going to take a quick picture of my  lunch and log it into the app this one's  serving a fried rice add to 2 of my  vegetable servings  it is also packed with complex carbs to  keep me full and satisfied  no more mindless mid-afternoon snacking  so be sure to try this recipe and take  it up with you to school or work as for  dinner I wanted a simple one pot dish  and to start introducing beans and  legumes into my diet so I tried the  warming rut  with beings what you need are one large  onion 2 garlic cloves 2 medium zucchinis  one red bell pepper and one eggplant all  roughly chopped 1 tbsp of olive oil  about 800 gram or 2 cans of crushed  tomatoes 1 can of white beans rinsed and  drained 1 tablespoon of balsamic vinegar  1/2 a teaspoon of ground cumin 1  teaspoon of dried mixed herbs and salt  and pepper to taste  heat olive oil over medium-high heat  lightly stir fry the onion and garlic  for about 2 minutes stir in the eggplant  zucchini and bell pepper cook for  another 5 minutes until vegetables start  to brown stir in the tomatoes beans for  Samak vinegar cumin dried herbs and salt  and pepper cover and cook for another 30  minutes and to vegetables are tender  don't forget to stir occasionally and  serve warm so I would recommend you to  make this dish in bulk freeze it up and  just reheat when you want to eat it for  dinner or lunch so let me just add that  into my dinner and I served it with two  slices of toasts and also tomato salsa  there you have it I've met my vegetable  goal and as for my snacks I had a bottle  of fruit smoothie when I was out a  protein shake after my workout and also  a handful of trail mix prior to my  workouts so basically at the end of the  day I get to track all my meals my  exercises have I drank enough water and  did I achieve my vegetable and also  fruit  goals which I did yay so guys I would  encourage you to download the lifestyle  app for free by clicking on the link in  my description box below I trust that  this app will help guide you through  your fitness journey and also help you  achieve your fitness goals what are your  fitness goals for 2017 do let me know in  the comments below  if you enjoy this video if you love the  recipes be sure to give it a thumbs up  share this meal time with your friends  and subscribe to my youtube channel for  more fun fit and a lot more exciting  this year guys I wish you all the love 